# Supabase Migrations

Tables live in `public`. The browser client uses the publishable key and the
project runs with RLS disabled — match that, don't fight it.

## File rules

- Name: `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_snake_case_name.sql`, one concern per file.
- Migrations are append-only. Never edit or reorder a file that may have been
  applied; add a new timestamped migration instead.
- No data manipulation inside a schema migration. Data arrives from the pipeline
  (`/api/network/build`) or the admin UI.
- End the file with `NOTIFY pgrst, 'reload schema';` so PostgREST picks it up.

## Idempotency

Every statement must survive a re-run:

```sql
ALTER TABLE public.products ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS brand TEXT;
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.network_nodes (...);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_network_nodes_type ON public.network_nodes(type);
```

Never `DROP` a column or table in a migration that also adds data — separate it,
and prefer leaving the old column in place over a destructive change.

## Shape conventions

- Log/run tables: `BIGINT GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY` +
  `TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()`.
- Graph tables: `id TEXT PRIMARY KEY`, `type TEXT NOT NULL`, `weight NUMERIC`.
- Free-form payloads are `JSONB` with `DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb` (or `'[]'::jsonb`).
- Child rows reference their run with `run_id BIGINT REFERENCES public.network_runs(id) ON DELETE CASCADE`.
- Index every column you filter on in an API route (`type`, `source`, `target`, `run_id`).

## Security

- For each new table: `ALTER TABLE public.<t> DISABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;`
  to stay consistent with existing tables.
- Supabase environment variables stay server-side. Never import the service-role
  key into a `'use client'` file.
